@@ -9322,3 +9322,4 @@ Did NOT modify research-roadmap.yaml or scripts/research_conductor.py. Did NOT p
 - 2026-06-18: PHASE B1 (ARC NORTH STAR; operator MANDATORY 2026-06-17; biggest reproducible-level upside) -- E3 DEEPER on the high-headroom cracked games with a LOOKAHEAD-FIDELITY GATE BEFORE planning (Mind-Studio arXiv:2606.16070): lp85 L6 + tu93 L5 + tn36 L8 (program-editor object-control) + tr87 L7, +1 each per Incremental-Progress Scoping. .405 (exp4383) stalled at world-model lookahead-fidelity 0.80-0.875 -- BELOW the threshold needed to plan deeper -- so this attempt's STATED forward difference is to raise fidelity FIRST: extend the existing world models / solvers (results/arc_e3/<game>/world_model.py, scripts/arc3_tn36_offline_solver.py, the tu93/lp85/tr87 solvers), run K-step LOOKAHEAD-FIDELITY checks, and REFINE the world model until fidelity >= ~0.95 (a HARD gate) BEFORE attempting the deeper level. Entropy-selected exploration traces + a lightweight per-game skill file. LOOP the four targets with a per-target checkpoint + hard per-target wall-time cap (breadth-of-progress beats all-or-nothing). The codex agent IS the proposer (NO nested CodexProposer). HARD gate per target: a NEW level offline_reproduced=true beyond the prior reproduced best (arc_solver_kit.reproduce). Report a per-target scorecard + the new reproducible_total_levels. An honest partial per target (best fidelity reached + the residual win-mechanic gap CLASS) is PROGRESS. verifier_is_oracle=true (execution-grounded). NO TRM training; NO leaderboard submission; checkpoint after EACH target. (⚠️ Research Finding) — honest_verdict=complete_e3_deeper_partial; results/experiment_4394_e3_deeper_fidelity_gate.json
 - 2026-06-18: PHASE B2 (ARC NORTH STAR; operator MANDATORY 2026-06-17; close the named hidden-rule gaps) -- E3 the BLOCKED-mechanic next-levels: ar25 L2 (action7 undo-stack) + ka59 L2 (step-counter HUD + object-RELEVANCE) + ft09 L2, +1 each per Incremental-Progress Scoping. ar25 L1 + ka59 L1 + ft09 L1 are SOLVED; the next levels are blocked on NAMED hidden-rule gaps. exp4384 (.405) added Mind-Studio lookahead but produced NO new levels. This attempt's STATED forward difference: fold in the OUTER-LOOP's fresh ka59 finding (the blocker is object-RELEVANCE, not clicks -- the latest commits f0b078247/6fba583c7: click-capable exploration is built+correct, multi-object push state has adaptive key-granularity, ka59 is doubly-blocked on which object matters) + a lookahead-fidelity gate per the named register (ar25 action7 undo-stack, ka59 step-counter HUD + object-relevance, ft09 residual). The codex agent IS the proposer (NO nested CodexProposer). HARD gate per game: a NEW level offline_reproduced=true beyond the prior best. An honest partial per game (refined model + the sharper residual gap CLASS) is PROGRESS. verifier_is_oracle=true (execution-grounded). NO TRM training; NO leaderboard submission; checkpoint after EACH game. (⚠️ Research Finding) — honest_verdict=complete_e3_ar25_ka59_ft09_partial; results/experiment_4395_e3_blocked_mechanic_tails_ar25_ka59_ft09.json
 - 2026-06-18: PHASE C (CONTINUOUS SELF-LEARNING; mandated per research-program.md; the LOCALIZER compounds; verifier_is_oracle=false) -- does the verifiable-process-data LOCALIZER SELF-IMPROVE / COMPOUND as labeled first-error traces accumulate? The .405 detector COMPOUNDED but WEAKLY (exp4385: localization-F1 0.371->0.387, AUROC saturated 0.986 -- little headroom). The .406 localizer (exp4392) has REAL headroom (the ensemble baseline is F1 0.096). Apply the exp4364/exp4385 compounding-curve discipline to the localizer: as verifiable-synthetic + REAL first-error labels accumulate, measure held-out first-error localization-F1 vs the accumulated-corpus SIZE (a monotone-improving learning curve), reproduction-gated, with a POSITIVE CONTROL (a from-scratch localizer on the full corpus = the ceiling) and a NO-LEARNING baseline (the .405 ensemble detector, F1 0.096). Emit localizer_compounds BARE bool := (held-out first-error localization-F1 rises with corpus size BEYOND the no-learning baseline, delta CI95-excl-0, AND the positive control confirms non-trivial ceiling headroom). verifier_is_oracle=false. A win = the localizer vehicle COMPOUNDS (it gets better with first-error data -- the self-learning headline on the axis that now has real headroom); a CLEAN null (the localizer saturates early) is decision-grade. If exp4392 built no localizer, FALL BACK to the ensemble-detector localization-compounding reading. Cached candidates, CPU, zero quota. NO TRM training. (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete: clean_saturated_null_localizer; results/experiment_4396_localizer_self_learning_compounds.json
+- 2026-06-18: PHASE D (CROSS-DOMAIN DETECTION CALIBRATION + POOL EXPANSION; complementary; cheap; verifier_is_oracle=false) -- scale the .405 cross-domain detection win (exp4386, GAP-4 ARC AUROC 0.963 on ONE non-FoVer domain) into a CALIBRATED multi-domain detector contract (arXiv:2102.10395). .405 reached only one non-FoVer domain (code/GSM pools 'unavailable until labeled verifier-score pools exist'); this builds them from EXISTING cached candidates and calibrates. Score the detector against FoVer + GAP-4 ARC + code (HumanEval, cached results/experiment_1999_code_verification_humaneval.json / exp2838 / exp2839 -- unit_test_pass_flags oracle, headroom 0.18) + GSM8K (cached adversarial_gsm8k_data_400.json / exp1998). Apply LEAVE-ONE-DOMAIN-OUT calibration (temperature / Platt scaling fit on the other domains) and report detection AUROC + risk-coverage (selective risk at coverage) + the SELECTION-headroom PER domain -- the headline is the DIVERGENCE (detect where you cannot select) + whether calibration TRANSFERS across domains. Emit detection_calibrated_multi_domain BARE bool := (detection AUROC CI95 lower bound > 0.5 on >=2 NON-FoVer domains AND leave-one-domain-out calibration keeps expected-calibration-error below the uncalibrated baseline on the held-out domain). verifier_is_oracle=false. A win = a deployable multi-domain detector contract (the verifier-domain-expansion step, north-star §0 step 2); a domain where detection ~= chance is LOGGED as a missing-verifier gap (the product backlog). This is cross-domain DETECTION (AUROC where selection headroom varies), NOT the RETIRED cross-domain SELECTION axis (exp4314). Cached candidates, CPU, zero quota. NO new live inference; NO TRM training. (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete: calibrated_multi_domain_contract_false; results/experiment_4397_cross_domain_detection_calibration.json
